{"name":"Inuit","hex":"#55a0b7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Inuit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of any of several Aboriginal peoples of coastal Arctic Canada, Alaska, and Greenland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of Inuk"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Inuit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inuit","blocks":[{"text":"Inuit are a group of culturally and historically similar Indigenous peoples traditionally inhabiting the Arctic and Subarctic regions of North America and Russia, including Greenland, Labrador, Quebec, Nunavut, the Northwest Territories, Yukon (traditionally), and Alaska. The Inuit languages are part of the Eskaleut languages, also known as Inuit-Yupik-Unangan and as Eskimo–Aleut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Distribution_of_Inuit_in_Canada_%282021%29.svg/330px-Distribution_of_Inuit_in_Canada_%282021%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit","wikidata":"Q189975"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/500px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/1280px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/500px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Sept